{
  "$schema-note": "Literal upstream iconify names -> b24-icons components, for the one case a port needs it: upstream HARDCODING an `i-lucide-*` string. Both projects define the same semantic icon keys (src/runtime/dictionary/icons.ts here, src/theme/icons.ts upstream), so a diff referencing `icons.<key>` needs no rewrite at all — see PORTING.md §1 for when that does and does not hold. Most rows are derived rather than chosen: for every key both sides define, the pair is (upstream's lucide name -> whatever this repo's dictionary maps that key to), and test/utils/icon-map.spec.ts re-checks that pairing. The rows that are judgement calls instead: circle-check (upstream's `success`, a key we lack — reuses copyCheck's glyph), circle-x (upstream's `error`, which our dictionary folds into `caution`), refresh-cw (our `refresh`, a key upstream lacks), terminal (upstream's only hardcoded literal, answered in prose/CodeIcon.vue), and activity/arrow-up-to-line/house/settings/user, which predate the derivation and match no key on either side. Upstream keys still without a row: eye, eyeOff, folder, folderOpen — pick a component during the port and add it here in the same commit (PORTING.md §4).",
